# Routes must match file paths

This repo uses the Next.js App Router. **Publicly reachable URL paths** should be derived from the **directory-relative path** of the corresponding route segments under `src/app/`; avoid "hand-written paths" that drift from the real directory structure.

## How to derive a URL

- Use `src/app/` as the root: each subsequent **folder name** (excluding file names like `page.tsx`, `layout.tsx`, `loading.tsx`, `error.tsx`, `route.ts`) forms a path segment in order, joined with `/`.
- **Route groups** — folder names like `(dashboard)`, `(marketing)` — **do not appear in the URL**; skip those segments when deriving the path.
- **Dynamic segments**: for folder names like `[id]` or `[slug]`, the URL contains the actual parameter value at that position; in docs or examples write `/.../:id` or describe the placeholder.
- **Optional / catch-all**: `[[...slug]]`, `[...slug]`, etc. map per Next.js conventions; do not invent a different scheme.

## When writing navigation and redirects

- `Link` `href`s, `redirect()`, `router.push`/`replace`, server-side `headers()`-related rewrites, breadcrumbs, sitemaps, etc. **should map one-to-one to the directory of the current or target `page.tsx`**; when adding a page, prefer **copying the href from the target file's parent path**, then add query/hash as needed.
- When a parallel directory structure already exists, do not maintain a separate "route constants table" that diverges from it as the primary source of truth; if constants already exist, **update them in sync when directories change**, or build them from path segments and keep them aligned with directory comments.
- For internal navigation prefer **in-app absolute paths starting with `/`** (matching the browser address bar), identical to the path derived from `src/app`; do not write the physical `src/app` path as a URL prefix (e.g. never `/src/app/...`).

## Examples

- Simulator UI source lives in the **separate repo** `keco-simulation`: `src/app/simulation-system/battle/skills/page.tsx`
  - URL: `/simulation-system/battle/skills`
- The main Keco repo keeps only the embed shell: `src/app/(dashboard)/simulation-system/[[...segments]]/page.tsx` → same URL (iframe loads the standalone app)
- File: `src/app/(dashboard)/projects/[projectId]/page.tsx`
  - URL: `/projects/:projectId` (replaced by the actual id at runtime)

## Anti-patterns

- The directory has moved to `battle/skills`, but a `Link` still points to the old `/battle-skill` or another path **with no matching folder chain under `src/app`**.
- Docs or comments describe routes **with spelling or nesting inconsistent with `src/app`**, making debugging harder.
